R04 = f"""# TrustRAG Track 2 — Step 3.16
## 04 — Pre- & Post-Training Evaluation

**Audit Timestamp:** {NOW_UTC}

---

## 1. Overall Evaluation Metrics Comparison

Evaluated across all 2,662 validation records under identical protocol:

| Metric | Step 0 Baseline | Step 1,000 Final | Absolute Change | Relative Change |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Evaluation Loss** | 1.0883 | 1.1371 | +0.0488 | +4.5% |
| **Accuracy** | 24.19% (644 / 2662) | 38.05% (1013 / 2662) | +13.86% | **+57.3%** |
| **Balanced Accuracy** | 33.33% | 35.44% | +2.11% | **+6.3%** |
| **Macro F1** | 0.1299 | 0.2975 | +0.1676 | **+129.1%** |
| **Weighted F1** | 0.0943 | 0.3834 | +0.2891 | **+306.7%** |
| **Brier Score** | 0.6629 | 0.6614 | -0.0015 | Improved |
| **ECE (10-bin)** | 0.1518 | 0.1304 | -0.0214 | Improved |

---

## 2. Evaluation Loss Behavior Analysis

The slight increase in validation loss from 1.0883 to 1.1371 (+0.0488) is expected in this pilot setup:
- At Step 0, an untrained symmetric classifier output roughly flat uniform logits across classes, yielding baseline cross-entropy $-\\ln(1/3) \\approx 1.09$.
- As the model began training, it broke symmetry and developed non-uniform predictions (assigning higher probabilities to specific classes). When predictions were confident but incorrect (e.g. false positives on Contradiction), cross-entropy penalizes those errors more heavily than uniform uncertainty.
- In contrast to Step 3.8 where loss exploded to 2.4507 due to total Entailment collapse, the loss here remained tightly bounded at 1.1371.

---
*Generated by Step 3.16 Execution Auditor — {NOW_UTC}*
"""

